---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="What's Your Sick Child Policy? | Marietta Childcare"
  description="Learn about Marietta Childcare's sick child policy, illness guidelines, and health requirements.">
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/diverse_children_sharing_toy_background.jpg" 
        alt="Sick child policy" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">What's Marietta Childcare's Sick Child Policy?</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Illness guidelines, when to keep children home, and health requirements for enrollment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto">
      <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Marietta Childcare's sick child policy protects the health of all children and staff. Marietta Childcare's illness guidelines ensure a safe, healthy environment for everyone.</p>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">When to Keep Children Home</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare requires that children with signs of illness remain home. Children should stay home from Marietta Childcare if they have a fever of 100.4°F or higher. Marietta Childcare's policy requires children to be fever-free for 24 hours without fever-reducing medication before returning.</p>
          <p>Children with contagious symptoms should not attend Marietta Childcare. Contagious symptoms that require staying home include cough, runny nose, sore throat, and body aches. Marietta Childcare's sick child policy protects all children from illness transmission.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Communicable Illness Guidelines</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare follows Georgia Department of Public Health guidelines for communicable illnesses. Communicable illnesses at Marietta Childcare include strep throat, pink eye, chicken pox, and hand-foot-mouth disease. Marietta Childcare's staff is trained to recognize symptoms of common communicable illnesses.</p>
          <p>Children with diagnosed communicable illnesses must follow specific return-to-care guidelines. Return-to-care requirements at Marietta Childcare vary by illness. Marietta Childcare's staff communicates specific requirements to families when illnesses are identified.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Health Screening at Drop-Off</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare conducts daily health checks at drop-off. Health screening at Marietta Childcare includes observation for signs of illness. Marietta Childcare's staff may ask questions about the child's health and any overnight symptoms.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare may request that children with signs of illness be picked up immediately. Health screening at Marietta Childcare protects all children from illness exposure. Marietta Childcare's daily health checks support a healthy environment.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Illness During Care</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare monitors children for signs of illness throughout the day. If a child becomes ill during care at Marietta Childcare, parents are contacted immediately. Marietta Childcare's staff provides comfort and care while waiting for pickup.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare isolates ill children from other children when possible. Isolation procedures at Marietta Childcare prevent illness transmission. Marietta Childcare's staff follows health protocols for managing illness during the day.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Medication Administration</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare does not administer fever-reducing medication to mask illness. Fever-reducing medication at Marietta Childcare is not given to allow children to attend. Marietta Childcare's policy ensures children are truly well before returning to care.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare can administer prescribed medications with proper authorization. Medication administration at Marietta Childcare follows strict protocols. Families must provide written authorization for all medications given at Marietta Childcare.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Immunization Requirements</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare requires current immunizations for all children. Immunization records at Marietta Childcare are maintained for each child. Marietta Childcare follows Georgia Department of Public Health immunization requirements.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare requires proof of immunizations during enrollment. Immunization updates at Marietta Childcare must be provided as children receive vaccines. Marietta Childcare's immunization requirements protect all children from preventable diseases.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Exclusion Criteria</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare has specific exclusion criteria for illness. Children are excluded from Marietta Childcare for fever, vomiting, diarrhea, and rash. Marietta Childcare's exclusion criteria follow public health guidelines.</p>
          <p>Exclusion at Marietta Childcare is temporary and based on specific health criteria. Children may return to Marietta Childcare once they meet return-to-care requirements. Marietta Childcare's exclusion policy protects children's health and prevents illness outbreaks.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Tuition During Illness</h2>
          <p>Families do not pay tuition at Marietta Childcare when children do not attend due to illness. Tuition refunds or credits at Marietta Childcare are provided for absences due to illness. Families should notify Marietta Childcare of illness-related absences.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's tuition policy supports families during illness. Tuition policies at Marietta Childcare are designed to be fair and family-friendly. Families should speak with the enrollment team about tuition during extended illness absences.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Communication About Illness</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare communicates with families about illness in the classroom. When illness is identified at Marietta Childcare, families are notified. Marietta Childcare's communication helps families monitor their children for symptoms.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare maintains confidentiality about individual children's illnesses. Communication at Marietta Childcare focuses on general illness notifications. Marietta Childcare's staff respects family privacy while protecting all children's health.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-blue-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Questions About Our Sick Child Policy?</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">Marietta Childcare welcomes questions about the sick child policy. Contact Marietta Childcare to discuss illness guidelines and how Marietta Childcare maintains a healthy environment.</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition">Contact Us</a>
        </section>

        <nav class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Pages</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li><a href="/faq/safety-security" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">How Safe Is Your Facility?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/faq/nutrition-meals" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">What About Meals and Snacks?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/programs" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Our Programs</a></li>
            <li><a href="/about" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">About Marietta Childcare</a></li>
            <li><a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Contact Marietta Childcare</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
